# MTG Database Schema Optimization and Integration Plan

## Goal
Optimize the MTG card database schema by replacing inefficient `TEXT` types with appropriate data types and normalizing the structure. This optimized schema will be integrated directly into the existing [pokemon](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/application/controllers/Admin.php#39-50) database in SQLyog to unify the store architecture.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The [assets/mtg.sql](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/assets/mtg.sql) file (152MB) is configured to create and use a separate [mtg](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/application/controllers/Store.php#58-69) database. To merge it into your [pokemon](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/application/controllers/Admin.php#39-50) database, please follow these steps:

1.  **Preparation**: Open [assets/mtg.sql](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/assets/mtg.sql) in a text editor.
2.  **Manual Edit**: Comment out or delete the following lines at the top:
    ```sql
    CREATE DATABASE /*!32312 IF NOT EXISTS*/`mtg` ...;
    USE `mtg`;
    ```
3.  **Import**: In SQLyog, select your [pokemon](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/application/controllers/Admin.php#39-50) database and run the modified [mtg.sql](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/assets/mtg.sql). This will create the `mtg_cards_raw` table inside [pokemon](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/application/controllers/Admin.php#39-50).
4.  **Optimization**: After the import finishes, run the `db/migrations/optimize_mtg_in_pokemon.sql` script (which I will provide) to transform the raw data into optimized tables.

## Proposed Changes

---

### Database Schema

#### [NEW] [optimize_mtg_in_pokemon.sql](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/db/migrations/optimize_mtg_in_pokemon.sql)
This script will:
- Create normalized tables: [mtg_cards](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/application/controllers/Admin.php#82-89), `mtg_card_colors`, `mtg_card_types`, `mtg_card_subtypes`, and `mtg_card_keywords`.
- Use `INSERT ... SELECT` with type casting (`CAST`, `CONVERT`) to move data from `mtg_cards_raw` to the new tables.
- Add primary keys, foreign keys, and indexes for performance.
- Rename the raw table to `mtg_cards_raw_old` once verification is complete.

---

### Application Logic

#### [MODIFY] [Store_model.php](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/application/models/Store_model.php)
Update the model to query the new [mtg_cards](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/application/controllers/Admin.php#82-89) table in the [pokemon](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/application/controllers/Admin.php#39-50) database.

#### [MODIFY] [database.php](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/application/config/database.php)
Remove the secondary [mtg](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/application/controllers/Store.php#58-69) database configuration since all data will now be in [pokemon](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/application/controllers/Admin.php#39-50).

